summary: Read all read-only sysfs and procfs entries continuously in QM container
description: |
  The goal of this test is to excercise the underlying kernel code that handles
  the sysfs and procfs entries when accessed, looking for possible
  interference with the ASIL-B environment.
  Test inputs:
    - Read only entries found using `find /sys -type f -not -perm /222` and `find /proc -type f -not -perm /222`.
  Expected results:
    - Test do not crash until it is stopped.
  Results location:
    - output.txt
contact: Pablo Ridolfi <pridolfi@redhat.com>
component:
  - kernel
framework: beakerlib
require:
  - tmux
duration: 3h
